---
description: Keep route screens thin; put feature UI in src/components and primitives in src/ui-components
alwaysApply: true
---

# Screen vs components vs ui-components

## `app/`

- Expo Router routes and layouts only. Each route file re-exports a screen: `export { default } from '@/screens/HomeScreen';`

## `src/screens/`

- **Only** route-level entry files: `*Screen.tsx` (default export for `app/` re-exports).
- **Do not** add hooks, mock data, utilities, or sub-view components next to `*Screen.tsx`. Move them to `src/components/<feature>/` or `src/hooks/` when shared.
- Screen files should be **thin**: render a single `*View` from `@/components/...`.

## `src/components/`

- Feature **screen bodies** (e.g. `ScanView`, `SearchView`), feature widgets, and **colocated** types/helpers for that feature.
- Subfolders by feature: `scan/`, `catalog/` (plus `home/` for the shell).
- May import from `@/ui-components/*`, `@/hooks/*`, `@/lib/*`, and other `@/components/...` modules.

## `src/ui-components/`

- **Brand primitives** reused across the app (`Text`, `Pill`, `ScreenHeader`, `cn`).
- Must stay generic: no feature copy, no data access. ESLint blocks imports of `@/components/*` and `@/lib/*` here.

## `src/lib/` and `src/hooks/`

- `lib/`: non-UI logic (`db/`, `embedding/`, `matching/`, `catalog/`), pure and unit-tested where possible. `lib` never imports UI.
- `hooks/`: shared hooks.

## Imports

Dependency direction: **`screens` → `components` → `ui-components`**; `components` and `hooks` may use `lib`.

When **creating** UI, compose from existing primitives and shared feature widgets — do not fork the same control on a second screen. See [compose-ui-components.mdc](compose-ui-components.mdc).
